  "result": "I fixed it: `--help` now lists short option names first, e.g. `-n, --name TEXT` instead of `--name, -n TEXT`.\n\nThe fix is the one-line change from the plan: I removed `reverse=True` from the sort in `join_options` (`src/click/formatting.py:319`).\n\n**Checks:**\n- I ran `--help` on a sample command with `--name` and `-n` and it now shows `-n, --name TEXT`.\n- The test suite gives the same result with and without the change: 1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed. pytest also reported 31,000 tests as deselected; I didn't pass any filter, so I don't know what's excluding them and they didn't run.\n\nBecause the tests pass either way, no current test checks this ordering, so it could come back unnoticed. I can add a small test in `tests/test_formatting.py` that checks the short name comes first if you'd like.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
